1
00:00:01,105 --> 00:00:03,545
<i>These two methods didn't work.</i>
<i>What the hell should I do now?</i>

2
00:00:03,625 --> 00:00:05,025
<i>"If there be one cursed by misfortune,</i>

3
00:00:05,105 --> 00:00:06,985
<i>then must another of good fortune</i>
<i>be sought out."</i>

4
00:00:07,065 --> 00:00:10,145
"The one of fortune must have
the moon as their ruling celestial body."

5
00:00:10,225 --> 00:00:11,985
-Yo, bro!
-Shit!

6
00:00:12,065 --> 00:00:13,265
Where did you come from?

7
00:00:13,345 --> 00:00:17,025
From now on,
I'll pick you up for university every day.

8
00:00:18,145 --> 00:00:19,465
-Deal, okay?
-Hey!

9
00:00:40,385 --> 00:00:43,785
Wow, you're getting better than me now.

10
00:00:43,865 --> 00:00:45,905
You could become a basketball player
when you grow up.

11
00:00:45,985 --> 00:00:47,065
Really, Dad?

12
00:00:47,145 --> 00:00:49,625
Of course.
Come on. Let's do it one more time.

13
00:00:53,065 --> 00:00:53,905
Ouch!

14
00:01:05,265 --> 00:01:06,385
Great job, son.

15
00:01:06,465 --> 00:01:08,265
No matter how many times we fall…

16
00:01:08,345 --> 00:01:10,745
-We have to get back up again.
-We have to get back up again.

17
00:01:24,905 --> 00:01:25,825
Hello?

18
00:01:25,905 --> 00:01:27,465
Are you done yet?

19
00:01:27,545 --> 00:01:28,825
Yeah, I'm done.

20
00:01:28,905 --> 00:01:31,105
<i>Hurry up. I booked a car already.</i>

21
00:01:31,705 --> 00:01:33,345
Something unlucky might happen
if you're alone.

22
00:01:33,425 --> 00:01:34,385
<i>Fine. Got it.</i>

23
00:01:39,505 --> 00:01:43,065
<i>Seriously, why are you</i>
<i>fussing over me so much?</i>

24
00:01:43,785 --> 00:01:44,665
Well…

25
00:01:45,465 --> 00:01:49,585
You just got hurt,
so I was worried about you.

26
00:01:49,665 --> 00:01:50,585
<i>Really?</i>

27
00:01:50,665 --> 00:01:52,905
-Yeah.
-Whoa, look. The comments are pouring in.

28
00:01:54,665 --> 00:01:56,145
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

29
00:01:59,465 --> 00:02:02,025
I know why you approached me now.

30
00:02:02,105 --> 00:02:03,145
Huh?

31
00:02:03,785 --> 00:02:05,585
You do?

32
00:02:11,585 --> 00:02:14,105
It's because you wanted
to make your ex jealous, right?

33
00:02:14,705 --> 00:02:15,585
Huh?

34
00:02:15,665 --> 00:02:17,785
You saw that Krit and I
are in the same faculty,

35
00:02:17,865 --> 00:02:20,265
so you're using me to get back at your ex.

36
00:02:21,065 --> 00:02:22,225
That's not true.

37
00:02:22,305 --> 00:02:23,945
I've never thought of doing that.

38
00:02:24,025 --> 00:02:25,305
I have my own reasons.

39
00:02:27,625 --> 00:02:30,545
Then what is it?

40
00:02:31,145 --> 00:02:32,825
Well, I…

41
00:02:33,785 --> 00:02:34,745
Just tell me.

42
00:02:35,625 --> 00:02:36,905
I…

43
00:02:39,065 --> 00:02:40,505
I…

44
00:02:45,265 --> 00:02:46,305
Hello?

45
00:02:46,385 --> 00:02:48,225
<i>Hello. Did you book a ride?</i>

46
00:02:48,305 --> 00:02:50,465
<i>You can come down now.</i>
<i>Traffic is getting heavy.</i>

47
00:02:52,825 --> 00:02:54,065
The car's here.

48
00:02:54,145 --> 00:02:55,105
Let's go now.

49
00:02:55,185 --> 00:02:57,745
You still haven't told me…

50
00:03:50,825 --> 00:03:52,425
Are you feeling any better?

51
00:03:52,505 --> 00:03:54,105
Well, a little.

52
00:03:55,545 --> 00:03:57,265
We're here.

53
00:03:59,225 --> 00:04:02,345
So, are you going to tell me
what your reason is?

54
00:04:03,865 --> 00:04:05,265
You're obsessed with this, aren't you?

55
00:04:05,345 --> 00:04:06,745
-Come on. Go to class.
-Wait.

56
00:04:07,945 --> 00:04:09,145
Are you coming to my class?

57
00:04:09,225 --> 00:04:10,825
Your faculty is over there.

58
00:04:11,825 --> 00:04:14,345
Oh, right.

59
00:04:14,985 --> 00:04:18,145
Don't forget that we're meeting
to work on the report this evening.

60
00:04:18,865 --> 00:04:19,705
Yeah.

61
00:04:30,865 --> 00:04:31,945
What's Rin doing here?

62
00:04:32,985 --> 00:04:34,345
Did he come to see me?

63
00:04:35,625 --> 00:04:37,785
Can't you see who Rin came here to meet?

64
00:04:39,465 --> 00:04:41,825
I don't know what you two are planning,

65
00:04:42,425 --> 00:04:44,145
but if you try to hurt Rin,

66
00:04:44,225 --> 00:04:45,745
I won't let you get away with it.

67
00:05:01,905 --> 00:05:02,745
What's going on?

68
00:05:08,225 --> 00:05:09,185
I think…

69
00:05:10,785 --> 00:05:12,945
I'm starting to believe what you told me.

70
00:05:13,545 --> 00:05:16,545
That Rin is dating him
just to get back at me.

71
00:05:17,305 --> 00:05:18,745
I don't feel good…

72
00:05:21,225 --> 00:05:22,705
about Rin dating that guy.

73
00:05:25,065 --> 00:05:29,665
Grass is not the strongest plant,

74
00:05:30,545 --> 00:05:37,305
but it is one of the toughest plants
in nature.

75
00:05:40,185 --> 00:05:42,745
If you don't stop staring at me,
I'll punch you.

76
00:05:47,425 --> 00:05:50,425
So you approached me
to make Krit jealous, right?

77
00:05:52,945 --> 00:05:53,785
Hey.

78
00:05:54,465 --> 00:05:56,345
I told you that's not true.

79
00:05:57,865 --> 00:05:59,865
Then what's your reason? Just tell me.

80
00:06:01,265 --> 00:06:02,625
I have my own reasons, okay?

81
00:06:04,865 --> 00:06:06,105
Then tell me.

82
00:06:08,265 --> 00:06:09,785
I'll tell you eventually.

83
00:06:12,705 --> 00:06:14,345
Just get back to the report.

84
00:06:14,865 --> 00:06:16,105
We brought so many books.

85
00:06:28,145 --> 00:06:34,065
Grass may not grow particularly tall.

86
00:06:34,865 --> 00:06:36,265
Finally, we're done.

87
00:06:38,705 --> 00:06:40,265
I'll send the file right away.

88
00:06:41,745 --> 00:06:42,585
Okay.

89
00:07:00,505 --> 00:07:03,825
Now all that's left is the presentation.
I'll divide the parts for us.

90
00:07:04,785 --> 00:07:05,625
Huh?

91
00:07:05,705 --> 00:07:07,905
No. You do the presentation.

92
00:07:07,985 --> 00:07:11,545
We can't do that. The professor said
everyone in the group has to present.

93
00:07:11,625 --> 00:07:12,785
Don't you remember?

94
00:07:16,225 --> 00:07:17,105
I won't do it.

95
00:07:17,785 --> 00:07:18,985
I'm embarrassed.

96
00:07:19,065 --> 00:07:19,905
Huh?

97
00:07:20,505 --> 00:07:22,825
No, you have to speak.

98
00:07:22,905 --> 00:07:27,305
This project is graded in two parts,
the written report and the presentation.

99
00:07:29,865 --> 00:07:32,545
I won't let us lose the presentation.

100
00:07:33,345 --> 00:07:35,905
No matter what, you have to present.

101
00:07:37,505 --> 00:07:38,665
No way!

102
00:07:39,665 --> 00:07:42,905
Air-purifying plants
can absorb toxins from the air

103
00:07:42,985 --> 00:07:46,345
through photosynthesis and gas exchange.

104
00:07:46,425 --> 00:07:49,225
They take in carbon dioxide
and release oxygen,

105
00:07:49,305 --> 00:07:52,745
gradually improving air quality.

106
00:07:52,825 --> 00:07:55,825
Also, don't forget
that placement is important.

107
00:07:55,905 --> 00:07:58,305
They should be placed
where there's sunlight or indirect light

108
00:07:58,385 --> 00:08:00,345
so they can photosynthesize efficiently.

109
00:08:00,425 --> 00:08:03,465
This allows the leaves to absorb toxins
and release oxygen.

110
00:08:04,065 --> 00:08:06,985
By surviving anywhere,
grass can improve its own value.

111
00:08:07,585 --> 00:08:09,385
-Thank you.
-Bravo!

112
00:08:09,465 --> 00:08:10,825
Great job!

113
00:08:12,265 --> 00:08:13,145
Well done.

114
00:08:13,745 --> 00:08:15,625
Okay. Next pair, please.

115
00:08:18,625 --> 00:08:19,705
Let's go.

116
00:08:27,585 --> 00:08:31,665
Grass is a small plant
that many people may overlook.

117
00:08:31,745 --> 00:08:36,585
But in fact, it is one
of the toughest living things in nature.

118
00:08:36,664 --> 00:08:39,144
It may not grow outstandingly tall,

119
00:08:39,225 --> 00:08:43,865
but what makes it special
is its ability to survive.

120
00:08:44,465 --> 00:08:48,745
Grass has its growing point
very close to the ground,

121
00:08:48,825 --> 00:08:54,665
which allows it to recover
even after being cut or stepped on.

122
00:08:55,265 --> 00:08:58,265
Is there anything
you'd like to add, Khobfa?

123
00:09:05,025 --> 00:09:06,105
Well…

124
00:09:11,025 --> 00:09:12,105
Well…

125
00:09:16,185 --> 00:09:17,585
Please give me a second.

126
00:09:20,225 --> 00:09:21,745
Relax, okay?

127
00:09:22,505 --> 00:09:24,905
You can do this. Don't overthink it.

128
00:09:27,625 --> 00:09:31,945
Just imagine you're telling a story
to someone you love.

129
00:09:35,105 --> 00:09:39,185
So, does your group
have anything else to add?

130
00:09:40,225 --> 00:09:41,065
Yes.

131
00:09:48,745 --> 00:09:51,225
RELATED STUDIES

132
00:09:52,785 --> 00:09:57,785
<i>Just imagine you're telling a story</i>
<i>to someone you love.</i>

133
00:10:03,025 --> 00:10:04,345
Grass…

134
00:10:15,585 --> 00:10:18,385
does not always grow
in the best conditions.

135
00:10:18,465 --> 00:10:22,545
No one takes care of it
or pays attention to it.

136
00:10:23,585 --> 00:10:25,745
But every time it falls,

137
00:10:25,825 --> 00:10:28,865
it still manages
to stand back up on its own.

138
00:10:29,625 --> 00:10:30,905
Sometimes,

139
00:10:32,265 --> 00:10:36,625
true strength may simply mean surviving

140
00:10:36,705 --> 00:10:39,185
in a world that has never been kind to us,

141
00:10:39,785 --> 00:10:43,465
just like grass that may seem worthless

142
00:10:44,505 --> 00:10:47,545
but still finds its own way to grow.

143
00:11:05,345 --> 00:11:06,705
GRASS GENETICS AND STRENGTH

144
00:11:18,065 --> 00:11:19,425
-Yay!
-Yay!

145
00:11:24,345 --> 00:11:25,225
How was it?

146
00:11:25,305 --> 00:11:27,625
You got praised by the professor,
and now you don't know how to act?

147
00:11:27,705 --> 00:11:29,265
You should thank me.

148
00:11:29,345 --> 00:11:31,905
I told you to end it on a strong note.

149
00:11:32,505 --> 00:11:33,945
I'm not used to this.

150
00:11:35,985 --> 00:11:38,625
That's how it is. See? I told you.

151
00:11:38,705 --> 00:11:41,345
Everyone does well
when they're with me, kiddo.

152
00:11:42,025 --> 00:11:43,585
Damn, you're bragging so much.

153
00:11:45,505 --> 00:11:46,785
Come to think of it,

154
00:11:47,505 --> 00:11:51,425
you look really good
when you put your mind to something.

155
00:11:52,705 --> 00:11:53,745
What?

156
00:11:53,825 --> 00:11:57,225
Huh? Don't you know?

157
00:11:57,305 --> 00:11:59,825
When someone is truly focused
on doing something,

158
00:11:59,905 --> 00:12:01,745
they look incredibly attractive.

159
00:12:05,425 --> 00:12:06,545
You're exaggerating.

160
00:12:07,265 --> 00:12:09,025
Go home already. I'm going to sleep.

161
00:12:14,825 --> 00:12:15,785
Go home already.

162
00:12:17,225 --> 00:12:18,065
Hey!

163
00:12:19,625 --> 00:12:20,665
Come on.

164
00:12:23,465 --> 00:12:25,105
Are you sure you can stay alone?

165
00:12:25,185 --> 00:12:26,705
What kind of question is that?

166
00:12:26,785 --> 00:12:28,185
I've always lived alone.

167
00:12:28,265 --> 00:12:29,385
Go home already.

168
00:12:39,825 --> 00:12:41,385
Jeez.

169
00:12:49,625 --> 00:12:50,865
Hey.

170
00:12:51,545 --> 00:12:52,545
What are you doing?

171
00:12:53,145 --> 00:12:54,385
Go home already.

172
00:13:03,985 --> 00:13:05,745
Fine. I'll go.

173
00:13:15,145 --> 00:13:16,705
Be careful, okay?

174
00:13:17,305 --> 00:13:18,145
Yeah.

175
00:13:30,625 --> 00:13:31,745
<i>What should I do?</i>

176
00:13:32,305 --> 00:13:33,665
<i>Whenever I'm not with him,</i>

177
00:13:33,745 --> 00:13:36,385
<i>I'm scared something unlucky</i>
<i>will happen to him again.</i>

178
00:13:36,945 --> 00:13:41,385
<i>Then you'll have to find a way</i>
<i>to stay with him 24 hours a day.</i>

179
00:13:41,465 --> 00:13:42,465
What?

180
00:13:47,905 --> 00:13:51,065
How am I supposed
to stay with him for 24 hours a day?

181
00:14:00,265 --> 00:14:01,665
Hello?

182
00:14:01,745 --> 00:14:04,185
<i>I found out you cursed me with bad luck.</i>

183
00:14:06,265 --> 00:14:07,385
Khobfa?

184
00:14:07,465 --> 00:14:10,985
<i>-Why the hell did you do that, asshole?</i>
-Khobfa? Where are you?

185
00:14:11,545 --> 00:14:13,065
I'm sorry.

186
00:14:21,465 --> 00:14:22,385
Khobfa!

187
00:14:24,065 --> 00:14:25,345
Hey!

188
00:14:26,665 --> 00:14:28,705
Hey, Khobfa!

189
00:14:31,145 --> 00:14:32,105
<i>Khobfa!</i>

190
00:14:33,705 --> 00:14:34,705
<i>Khobfa!</i>

191
00:14:35,585 --> 00:14:36,585
Khobfa!

192
00:14:36,665 --> 00:14:37,705
Khobfa!

193
00:14:41,465 --> 00:14:43,625
Khobfa!

194
00:14:43,705 --> 00:14:46,105
You're safe, right?
Nothing unlucky happened, right?

195
00:14:46,185 --> 00:14:47,585
Well, not really.

196
00:14:47,665 --> 00:14:51,065
I just got a little electric shock
from an iron

197
00:14:51,145 --> 00:14:54,465
and fell on the balcony.

198
00:14:56,305 --> 00:14:59,025
Khobfa! Those are all unlucky!

199
00:14:59,105 --> 00:15:00,745
Unlucky? What the hell?

200
00:15:04,825 --> 00:15:07,105
Why did you call us here? What's going on?

201
00:15:08,665 --> 00:15:10,785
Well, I think…

202
00:15:11,585 --> 00:15:13,465
I'm going to become Khobfa's roommate.

203
00:15:13,545 --> 00:15:14,465
-Huh?
-Huh?

204
00:15:15,545 --> 00:15:16,865
Can you at least give us a reason?

205
00:15:19,185 --> 00:15:20,385
I can't tell you yet.

206
00:15:20,465 --> 00:15:21,305
What?

207
00:15:22,705 --> 00:15:24,385
Oh, I know.

208
00:15:26,025 --> 00:15:27,905
You're trying
to make your ex jealous, right?

209
00:15:27,985 --> 00:15:28,905
Huh?

210
00:15:28,985 --> 00:15:32,305
You saw Krit flirting with Mochi,
and you couldn't stand it.

211
00:15:33,865 --> 00:15:36,345
-That has to be it.
-I think so too.

212
00:15:36,425 --> 00:15:38,065
-I don't think so.
-It is!

213
00:15:38,145 --> 00:15:39,785
Good job, my friend.

214
00:15:58,505 --> 00:16:00,665
Let me be your roommate, Khobfa.

215
00:16:00,745 --> 00:16:01,585
What?

216
00:16:01,665 --> 00:16:03,705
My friend suddenly told me
to find somewhere else to live.

217
00:16:03,785 --> 00:16:05,545
The owner of our current place
wants the house back.

218
00:16:05,625 --> 00:16:06,625
Can I stay for a while?

219
00:16:06,705 --> 00:16:08,105
No.

220
00:16:09,065 --> 00:16:10,665
Come on.

221
00:16:10,745 --> 00:16:12,305
Please help me.

222
00:16:12,385 --> 00:16:14,505
I really don't know where else to go.

223
00:16:14,585 --> 00:16:15,945
It happened so suddenly.

224
00:16:16,545 --> 00:16:18,425
Why don't you stay
with one of your friends?

225
00:16:19,025 --> 00:16:23,305
All my friends have gone back home,
but I don't have a home in Bangkok.

226
00:16:23,385 --> 00:16:24,745
Please.

227
00:16:24,825 --> 00:16:25,745
How about this?

228
00:16:25,825 --> 00:16:27,265
I'll help you with all your work.

229
00:16:27,345 --> 00:16:29,425
Whatever assignments you have,
I'll help you with everything.

230
00:16:30,745 --> 00:16:31,825
No.

231
00:16:35,425 --> 00:16:36,545
Why?

232
00:16:38,385 --> 00:16:39,745
I don't want a roommate.

233
00:16:43,105 --> 00:16:44,825
You're so heartless!

234
00:16:47,385 --> 00:16:48,825
What now?

235
00:16:48,905 --> 00:16:50,545
We already worked together on the project.

236
00:16:51,145 --> 00:16:53,065
From now on, can you stop bothering me?

237
00:17:02,785 --> 00:17:03,785
Damn.

238
00:17:06,665 --> 00:17:09,145
Hey, be kind to me, okay?

239
00:17:11,865 --> 00:17:13,905
TOP 5 FINALISTS
PITCHING BUSINESS MODEL COMPETITION 2026

240
00:17:13,985 --> 00:17:16,745
Hey, your name is on it.

241
00:17:18,505 --> 00:17:20,065
You made it to the next round.

242
00:17:20,785 --> 00:17:21,625
Whoa.

243
00:17:22,224 --> 00:17:23,464
MR. KRITCHAPHAT LAMCHAISREE

244
00:17:23,545 --> 00:17:25,585
Krit's name is there too.

245
00:17:31,145 --> 00:17:32,545
Wow.

246
00:17:33,225 --> 00:17:38,145
The winner gets 300,000 baht
and 20 extra points.

247
00:17:38,985 --> 00:17:40,345
That's great.

248
00:17:44,625 --> 00:17:46,185
Why don't you look happy?

249
00:17:46,265 --> 00:17:47,905
I am happy.

250
00:17:47,985 --> 00:17:50,545
But I still have to do the pitch.

251
00:17:53,305 --> 00:17:54,825
What are you afraid of?

252
00:17:54,905 --> 00:17:56,745
Look who's right beside you.

253
00:17:56,825 --> 00:17:58,545
It's me, Rin.

254
00:17:58,625 --> 00:18:00,705
I'll coach you myself. Trust me.

255
00:18:00,785 --> 00:18:01,785
Don't you remember?

256
00:18:01,865 --> 00:18:04,185
The last time I coached you,
the professor praised you.

257
00:18:04,265 --> 00:18:05,745
You'll really coach me?

258
00:18:05,825 --> 00:18:08,065
But I have one condition.

259
00:18:08,145 --> 00:18:10,265
If you win,

260
00:18:10,785 --> 00:18:12,065
let me be your roommate.

261
00:18:14,505 --> 00:18:15,585
Then…

262
00:18:17,745 --> 00:18:18,865
never mind.

263
00:18:18,945 --> 00:18:20,345
Thanks anyway.

264
00:18:21,065 --> 00:18:23,505
Hey, come on!

265
00:18:23,585 --> 00:18:25,825
I was trying to help, Khobfa!

